 "notes": [
  "Registers are read with function 03 (holding). Function 04 (input registers) is also accepted and returns the same registers. The guide lists no write function.",
  "32-bit floats put the least significant word at the listed register (CDAB). The guide states this and its worked read example (607.6 ppm) confirms it.",
  "Unavailable data reads as quiet NaN (float) or 0x8000 (16-bit integer) rather than an exception.",
  "The 6401-6659 block repeats the readings with temperature in °F.",
  "Left out: error code register 514, a 32-bit integer meant for Vaisala support; the guide states the word order only for 32-bit floats.",
  "DIP-switch address 0 puts the device offline (Modbus disabled).",
  "Left out: text string test register 7940, because the guide does not give its length in registers."
 ],
